# agi — provider credentials. THIS FILE IS THE SHAPE. IT HOLDS NO VALUES.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env && $EDITOR .env
#
# `.env.example` is committed and is graph content: `level3.py` mints a build
# node for it like any other tracked file, so the *shape* of the secret set —
# which keys the loop needs, what each is for — is versioned, reviewable, and
# carried to every clone. `.env` is gitignored, mode 0600, and never leaves the
# box it was typed on. A value change is invisible to git and to the grid; a
# SHAPE change (a key added or retired, here) is a version. That asymmetry is
# the point, not a gap.
#
# Read by:
#   - `driver.sh`, which sources `.env` after resolving the project and before
#     any dispatch, so pi and every child process inherits these.
#   - `~/.pi/agent/auth.json`, via `extensions/agi/bin/env-get.sh`, so pi
#     resolves the same one file even when launched by hand.

# OpenRouter — paid provider for pi-runtime kids.
# Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys        pi provider id: openrouter
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional. pi already stores a MiniMax key in ~/.pi/agent/auth.json; set one
# here only if this file should become the single source for it too.
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# NEVER set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or any CLAUDE_CODE_* var in this file.
# `dispatch.py` scrubs exactly those from pi child environments on purpose: if
# pi inherits them, every spawned subagent silently bills the interactive
# Claude Code subscription and competes with the session for its quota. Putting
# one here re-adds that leak from below the scrub, where nothing checks.
